    <p>
      <strong>Proof of Corollary <a href="/tag/4E7EDF" data-tag="4E7EDF">5.2.6.5</a>.</strong>
       The first claim follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/209940" data-tag="209940">5.2.6.3</a>. To prove the second, we may assume without loss of generality that $\calD $ is minimal, so that $\calD $ is union of small full subcategories $\{  \calD _{\alpha } \} $. It will suffice to show that, for each index $\alpha $ such that $f$ factors through $\calD _{\alpha }$, the restricted transformation $f \rightarrow ((F \circ G)| \calD _{\alpha }) \circ f$ exhibits $(F \circ G)| \calD _{\alpha }$ as a left Kan extension of $f$ along the induced map $\calC \rightarrow \calD _{\alpha }$, which follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/68A5AF" data-tag="68A5AF">5.2.6.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
